{"source": "tts:kokoro:af_heart", "precision": "tts", "offset": 0, "duration": 147.256, "sentences": [{"text": "Fifteen containers run hareet.ai in production.", "start": 0, "end": 3.067}, {"text": "Here's what each one does, why it's there, and what happens when it fails.", "start": 3.317, "end": 6.967}, {"text": "The edge is the only door: nginx, unprivileged, listening on six ports, all on the machine's own loopback address.", "start": 7.217, "end": 14.498}, {"text": "If it fails, nothing can reach the stack, but the stack keeps running, and the meter keeps its state.", "start": 14.747, "end": 19.941}, {"text": "Behind it, web serves the room.", "start": 20.192, "end": 21.969}, {"text": "If web is down, the edge answers with its own page: \"The room is unavailable right now.\"", "start": 22.218, "end": 27.437}, {"text": "The gateway is the brain: routing, the meter, the kill switch, and every alert.", "start": 27.688, "end": 32.023}, {"text": "It's the only container with a road out.", "start": 32.272, "end": 34.317}, {"text": "If it fails, the edge answers \"unavailable\", nothing is spent, and alerts wait in the outbox until it's back.", "start": 34.567, "end": 41.063}, {"text": "Gateway-state is the gateway's own database: the meter, the switch, the ledger, the audit log.", "start": 41.313, "end": 46.74}, {"text": "If it can't be reached, every request fails closed at once, and after sixty seconds, one alert goes out.", "start": 46.991, "end": 53.066}, {"text": "The model server is llama dot cpp, on the GPU.", "start": 53.315, "end": 56.857}, {"text": "Nothing waits on it.", "start": 57.108, "end": 58.269}, {"text": "If it's down, the gateway notices within a second and answers from the capped paid fallback;", "start": 58.519, "end": 63.657}, {"text": "if that's down too, the answer is the degraded line, and an alert says so.", "start": 63.907, "end": 68.3}, {"text": "Then the eyes.", "start": 68.55, "end": 69.463}, {"text": "The OpenTelemetry collector strips prompts and answers out of the telemetry, then sends metrics to Prometheus, logs to Loki, and traces to Langfuse.", "start": 69.712, "end": 79.14}, {"text": "If it fails, exports stop, a freshness panel shows how stale the data is, and enforcement never notices.", "start": 79.391, "end": 86.201}, {"text": "Prometheus keeps thirty days of metrics, Loki thirty days of the gateway's logs, and Grafana draws them on one read-only dashboard.", "start": 86.451, "end": 94.742}, {"text": "The alerts that guard the budget are the gateway's job, on Telegram first, then email, and they never wait on a dashboard.", "start": 94.992, "end": 101.831}, {"text": "And every day, a summary reports the CPU metrics, with alerts based on them too.", "start": 102.081, "end": 107.087}, {"text": "Langfuse keeps the traces, and it takes six containers: its web app and a worker, its own Postgres, ClickHouse for the traces, Valkey for the queue, and SeaweedFS for storage.", "start": 107.337, "end": 118.355}, {"text": "If any of them fails, traces arrive late, or are dropped after ten minutes of retries, and a panel counts the drops.", "start": 118.605, "end": 125.699}, {"text": "The twin keeps answering.", "start": 125.949, "end": 127.273}, {"text": "Every container runs with no new privileges, on a network with no route out.", "start": 127.522, "end": 132.052}, {"text": "Only the edge listens, and only the gateway leaves.", "start": 132.302, "end": 135.205}, {"text": "And every alert names its runbook: what you see, what it means, what to do, how to check, how to undo, and what to record.", "start": 135.455, "end": 142.55}, {"text": "Fifteen containers, one command.", "start": 142.8, "end": 144.663}, {"text": "Built in the open, at hareet dot A I.", "start": 144.913, "end": 147.255}], "words": [{"word": "Fifteen", "start": 0, "end": 0.369}, {"word": "containers", "start": 0.369, "end": 0.922}, {"word": "run", "start": 0.922, "end": 1.107}, {"word": "hareet.ai", "start": 1.107, "end": 2.329}, 